A||||4||kimmer_catlady||4Th gear won't work!!!
Z||000000||kimmer_catlady||08-04-99||11:48 PM||||I have a 85 2m4 and it does nothing but break down constantly.  I was driving on the highway today when the 4th gear decided not to work.  I even tried double clutching it, but that didn't work.  What sould I be looking for here?  Also, the spedo crapped out on me for no good reason, someone mentioned replacing the VSS, but could it be grounding problems and if so, which wires, where?  ALSO, various dash lights come on for some strange reason at wierd times.  ALSO, (yes I own a lemon), there are dead spots somentimes right before I shift gears (that's before the 4th gear decided to not work).  I need some serious help here!  Nobody seems to know how to fix any of this stuff.
Z||000001||DJRice||08-05-99||07:39 AM||||I'll go out on a limb here, but If you dont have 4th gear, the speedo doesnt work, and you have dead spots before you shift gears, you may have major transmission problems.<p>What dash lights come on?
Z||000002||theogre||08-05-99||08:28 AM||||the speedo runs off an output shaft that is geared to the right axle. It's independant of the tranny main internals.<p>It could be worn out linkages, clutch problems, and/or internal problems in the tranny. I don't know what you mean by dead spots. If you mean that it feels like the car is sudenly losing power, like you pressed the clutch to soon, as the engine winds up the RMP range it could be the clutch slipping. 
Z||000003||ChadMan||08-05-99||11:34 AM||||Check your shifter cables.  I once lost 3rd gear in my 84 Coupe and it turned out to be a retaining clip that held the shifter cables in place at the transmission end.  The cable would just flail around when I tried to shift into 3rd.  $2 and 15 minutes and I was back in business.  Kimmer, hope you're this lucky.
Z||000004||kimmer_catlady||08-05-99||02:37 PM||||Okay!  We are getting somewhere here!  Found out why speedo wasn't working - the "mechanic" who checked my tranny fluid pushed the blue plastic gear on the end of the VSS into the transmission when he replaced it. So much for going to the professionals!  The tranny linkage is loose and I have ordered the parts needed for the repair from the States; I wondered if any one knew of a way to fix loose linkage for the short term?
